# Copy this file to .env, in this folder, and paste your keys in THAT copy.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# ⚠️ Keep this file's values EMPTY. It is the template, and unlike .env it is
# NOT gitignored — a key pasted here is a key that gets committed, pushed and
# submitted with the project. If you have already done it, clear the value and
# rotate the key rather than assuming nobody noticed.
#
# Both of these are SECRETS, unlike the app's Clerk publishable key. They are
# billable and they must never reach the phone: anything named EXPO_PUBLIC_* is
# inlined into the app bundle at build time and can be read out of a shipped
# app. That is exactly why these calls live in this service instead of in the
# app.
#
# service/.env is gitignored. Do not commit it, and do not paste a key into
# chat, a screenshot, or the project README.
#
# Each key powers one endpoint and nothing else. Missing either one returns 503
# from that endpoint — a setup problem, not a failure — and everything else
# keeps working.

# POST /analyse — reading a garment out of a photograph.
# Free from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# POST /try-on — CatVTON, hosted on fal (see tryon.py).
# From https://fal.ai/dashboard/keys
FAL_KEY=
